    "mission_1.sketch": {
      "data": "",
      "mime": "image/png",
      "source": "canvas"
    },
    "mission_1.trial_synthesis": "All three trials mostly matched my predictions. Trial 1 moved straight with no heading change. Trial 2 turned left and then moved forward. Trial 3 followed a curved path while turning left. The largest difference was in Trial 3's heading, which was 0.081 rad less than predicted. A possible cause is that the robot turned slightly slower than expected. Odometry speed and timing data could help test this. At the same speed of 0.15 m/s for twice the Trial 1 duration (6 seconds), the straight-line distance would be 0.90 m.",
    "mission_2.frame_context": "The rear camera stays fixed because it is physically attached to the robot, so its position and rotation relative to base_link do not change. The hallway camera is fixed in the environment, not on the robot. As the robot moves, its position and orientation relative to the hallway camera change, so the transform to base_link changes.",
    "mission_2.improved_changes": "The improved prompt clearly specifies hall_camera as the source and base_link as the target. It uses the point's timestamp and the TF buffer instead of hard-coded offsets. If the transform is unavailable, it returns None without moving the robot.\n",
    "mission_2.initial_analysis": "The AI assumed the camera and robot frame names. It did not properly explain timestamps or what to do if the TF transform was unavailable. It also did not need to use any robot motion topics.\n",
    "mission_2.initial_output": "To convert a point from the hallway camera frame to the robot's `base_link` frame, use ROS 2 `tf2`. Create a `tf2_ros.Buffer` and `TransformListener`, then look up the transform between the two frames and transform the point.\n\n```python\nimport rclpy\nfrom rclpy.node import Node\nimport tf2_ros\nfrom geometry_msgs.msg import PointStamped\n\nclass PointTransformer(Node):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__('point_transformer')\n\n        self.tf_buffer = tf2_ros.Buffer()\n        self.tf_listener = tf2_ros.TransformListener(\n            self.tf_buffer, self\n        )\n\n    def transform_point(self, point):\n        try:\n            transform = self.tf_buffer.lookup_transform(\n                'base_link',\n                'hallway_camera',\n                rclpy.time.Time()\n            )\n\n            transformed = tf2_ros.do_transform_point(\n                point, transform\n            )\n\n            return transformed\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            self.get_logger().error(f'Transform failed: {e}')\n            return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    rclpy.init()\n    node = PointTransformer()\n\n    point = PointStamped()\n    point.header.frame_id = 'hallway_camera'\n    point.point.x = 1.0\n    point.point.y = 0.0\n    point.point.z = 0.0\n\n    result = node.transform_point(point)\n\n    if result:\n        print(result)\n\n    node.destroy_node()\n    rclpy.shutdown()\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
    "mission_2.initial_prompt": "Write ROS 2 Python code that converts a point detected by the hallway camera into the robot's base_link frame.\n",
    "mission_2.initial_source": "import rclpy\nfrom rclpy.node import Node\nimport tf2_ros\nfrom geometry_msgs.msg import PointStamped\nfrom tf2_geometry_msgs import do_transform_point\n\nclass PointTransformer(Node):\ndef **init**(self):\nsuper().**init**('point_transformer')\nself.tf_buffer = tf2_ros.Buffer()\nself.tf_listener = tf2_ros.TransformListener(self.tf_buffer, self)\n\ndef transform_point(self, point):\n    try:\n        transform = self.tf_buffer.lookup_transform(\n            'base_link',\n            'hallway_camera',\n            rclpy.time.Time()\n        )\n        return do_transform_point(point, transform)\n    except Exception as e:\n        self.get_logger().error(f'Transform failed: {e}')\n        return None\n\ndef main():\nrclpy.init()\nnode = PointTransformer()\n\npoint = PointStamped()\npoint.header.frame_id = 'hallway_camera'\npoint.point.x = 1.0\npoint.point.y = 0.0\npoint.point.z = 0.0\n\nresult = node.transform_point(point)\n\nif result:\n    print(result)\n\nnode.destroy_node()\nrclpy.shutdown()\n\nif **name** == '**main**':\nmain()\n",
    "mission_2.live_issue": "",
